    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0160" n="44" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg44"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 825.20/21A.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 15.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 14, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform you that the
                    following joint resolution, previously passed by the Senate, was passed on the
                    6th <pb facs="0161" n="45" xml:id="pg45"/> instant by the House of
                    Representatives and was signed by the President on May 11, 1912: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Resolved, etc.</hi>, That Capt. John W. Gulick,
                            Coast Artillery Corps, United States Army, be, and he is hereby,
                            permitted to accept from the Government of the Republic of Chile the
                            position of instructor of the Coast Artillery of the Chilean Army and
                            the emoluments, rights and privileges pertaining thereto.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>This information has already been telegraphed to the American Legation at
                    Santiago.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
